<div class="note"><b>AI NOTE</b> &mdash; PROVISIONAL machine alignment by Codex, independent English-first proposal. Distinguish two victim/death occurrences and a final other-person/victim reference. Mi byung/cannot occur is the genuine negative predicate at d3, avoiding any unsupported not-inside-cannot convention. Ma and bar around the first shi contribute jointly to before and remain unbanked; there is no invented absent-negation null. Mnyam du owns the attested temporal idiom at the same time. Body and stage anaphors are not forced onto repeated English nouns; exact source and GMR English are preserved.</div>
